The interview process was very detailed and focused on practical, real-time DevOps experience.
They mainly asked questions around:

🔹 AWS
🔹 GCP
🔹 GitLab CI/CD
🔹 Docker
🔹 Kubernetes
🔹 Terraform

Here are some of the important questions he was asked 👇

AWS Questions
What is the difference between Security Groups and NACLs?
 How does Auto Scaling work and how do you troubleshoot scaling issues?
Explain how ALB and NLB work internally.
 What is VPC Peering? Can we do transitive peering?
 How do you secure sensitive data in S3?

 GCP Questions
 What are VPC networks and how are they different from AWS VPC?
Explain GKE components.
How does Cloud Build work in GCP?
 What are preemptible VMs and when do we use them?
How do IAM roles differ in GCP compared to AWS?

 GitLab CI/CD Questions
 Explain the GitLab CI pipeline stages.
 What is the purpose of .gitlab-ci.yml?
 How do you implement environment-specific deployment in GitLab?
 How do GitLab runners work?
 Difference between shared runners and group runners.

 Docker Questions
 What happens internally when you run docker run?
 Explain Docker layered architecture.
 How do you troubleshoot container memory leaks?
 Difference between Dockerfile COPY vs ADD.
 How to reduce Docker image size using multistage builds?

 Kubernetes Questions
 Explain the difference between Deployment, DaemonSet and StatefulSet.
 What happens when you run kubectl apply?
 How does the Kubernetes scheduler work?
 Explain liveness and readiness probes.
How do you debug CrashLoopBackOff issues?

 Terraform Questions
 What is the difference between terraform plan and terraform apply?
 How does the Terraform state file work internally?
 What are Terraform workspaces and when do you use them?
 How do you handle sensitive variables in Terraform?
 What is the difference between locals, variables, and outputs?

 The interview was highly scenario-based, focusing on problem-solving and real-time troubleshooting.


